WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.238
The second half of the gap table is about
what happens once you add real work.

2
00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:07.518
If your added step fails,
Learn's definition sends nothing,

3
00:00:07.518 --> 00:00:11.825
so the workflow sits there for the whole
wait before it calls the task failed.

4
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:14.588
There's no protection
against doing the work twice.

5
00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:17.278
The subject's name, email and manager land

6
00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:19.888
in run history for anyone who can read it.

7
00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:24.255
The retries are implicit, and the
authorization policy is typed by hand,

8
00:00:24.255 --> 00:00:27.512
with a placeholder value
that would block every call.

9
00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:30.500
The program's definition closes each one.
